// D4348 — a CALL RESULT of an inline value union with a function arm, delivered as is. The
// callee's tail yields the closure arm, and the classifier read that tail over its concrete
// union annotation, so the call passed for a bare closure and an un-annotated parameter it
// reached had no pin.
//
// The PROOF discriminates: the function arm must test true AND the string arm false, so a
// fold of either test to a constant prints `9`, never `2`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function mk(n: i32): ((x: i32) => i32) | string {
  if n == 0 { return "s" }
  return (x: i32) => x + n
}
// @@VALUE@@
mk(1)
// @@TYPE@@
((x: i32) => i32) | string
// @@FALLBACK@@
mk(2)
// @@TEST@@
!(v is string) && v is (x: i32) => i32
// @@HIT@@
print(2)
// @@MISS@@
print(9)
// @@WANT@@
2
